Z||000003||p4n1c||11-18-2001||04:13 PM||||The X-Box is definitly not a better system all around.  The graphics are no more better then my computer(which is using a GeForce2 MX-400), the 8 gig drive is for the patches that will be continously coming out for the buggy games.  The X-Box has crashed numerous times at the kiosks and even one here at Yorkdale mall in Toronto started to smoke.  The controller for it is a bad rip off of the Dreamcast controller, and very uncomfortable to hold.  So if you want an oversized, 9lb vcr looking paper weight to burn your house down, then by all means, go ahead.<P>The GameCube(using the next-gen ATi GPU) has far superior graphics and will have far superior games, and with the cheaper price of the GameCube, more people will buy it.  Nintendo is not in trouble with this system, nor have they ever been with any of their systems.  They have the backing of the developers, and a very large fan base.||||reg||1
