Z||000009||GTFiero1||11-18-2001||07:04 PM||||u <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by p4n1c:<P>The GameCube(using the next-gen ATi GPU) has far superior graphics and will have far superior games, and with the cheaper price of the GameCube, more people will buy it.  Nintendo is not in trouble with this system, nor have they ever been with any of their systems.  They have the backing of the developers, and a very large fan base.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>gah, what have you been reading? x-box is rated the fastest and best of all of the systems so far. they are all 128 bits so graphics arent really gonna be different. its speed that is affected and X-box is way faster than game cube. i am playing game cube right now and i must say the contoller is horrible m hand is cramped up...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||p4n1c||11-18-2001||07:28 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTFiero1:<BR><B>u <BR>gah, what have you been reading? x-box is rated the fastest and best of all of the systems so far. they are all 128 bits so graphics arent really gonna be different. its speed that is affected and X-box is way faster than game cube. i am playing game cube right now and i must say the contoller is horrible m hand is cramped up...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL!  If you think 128-bits is the deciding factor in graphics rendering, you are sadly mistaken.  My Rage128 is 128-bits, but it is blown away by my GeForce2 MX-400 which is also 128-bits.  My friends Radeon blows away my GeForce2 and it is also 128-bit. And so on and so forth.<P>The GameCube has far superior graphics to the X-Box.  ATi has always had the superior hardware to nVidia.<P>The reviews are already coming out that X-Box will be left in the dust, next to GameCube and the older then the two PS2.<P>The GameCube controller feels nice in my hand, it felt very comfortable, just like the N64 controller.  The X-Box controller was this big cumbersome controller that was a blantant ripoff of Dreamcasts controller, but done horribly worse.<P>"An interesting thing to note about the Gamecube, <B>relating to those problems XBox was having with overheating in display stands</B>: this thing doesn't get hot. I was playing for a good 4 hours straight the other day (one of my shorter stretches) and I went up and touched the Gamecube, out of curiosity, and all I could find was a slightly warm spot on the bottom. The huge vents in the side do their job well. To be fair, it was prettly close to a window, but it's still insane compared to my N64 or PSX. Anyway, yeah. "<P>[EDIT: Added slashdot user comment on heat with the GameCube vs. X-Box"]<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 11-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||p4n1c||11-18-2001||07:31 PM||||Here is what my friend writes(he is a game-a-holic):<P>"The fact that M$ needed to use a FASTER CPU than Gamecube to acheive the same graphics level is pathetic. If Nintendo can put out graphics like this with a slower processor, imagine what they can do if they went to the store like M$ did and ask for as many P3s they could get their hands on... I think it's pretty obvious that M$ hadn't put much thought into their system and decided to go with something they could just slap together in half an hour and not test it properly.<P>Also, lets look at M$'s track record. CRAP. Well, let's see where Xbox goes then shall we? <P>The fact that they had to include a damn HD in the system tells you right away to be ready to be downloading fixes every week. <P>Just the fact that Nintendo went ahead and dished out so much money just for R&D on the GameCube, and went so far as to have their own hardware custom designed shows you just how much effort and thought they put into this thing."||||reg||1
