Z||000028||falconhulk||11-19-2001||01:34 PM||||nah turbo16 and the genisis were at the same time.  The genisis was a great system.  So was the dreamcast.  games were great.  Developers just would not back it.  It really sucks as the DC had some of the best games ever.  Games that PS2 owners are dying to get thier hands on!  ||||reg||1
Z||000029||p4n1c||11-19-2001||01:43 PM||||Sorry, you are right.  It does use the Windows 2000 kernel.  But it's not a PC right? lol!||||reg||10
Z||000030||falconhulk||11-19-2001||01:54 PM||||So what if its based on a PC?  I like PC's!  I like a PC/dvd player for $300.  It has a PC graphics card.  It has an intel 700 mhz processor.  It has a harddrive.  it has a DVD drive.  Thing is now you have a broad based PC like platform.  the reason a lot of PC games have bugs is that they must me able to run on 1000 diffrent hardware configs.  What runs on a 400mhz p2 must run on a 2 ghz p4.  Throw in all the video cards and driver versions.  Thats a mess.  thats the reason for patches.  A single platoform cuts that down.   Also the graphics will look better becasue nothing has to be toned down for lower level systems.  Sounds like a great idea to me.  It would to you to if you just thought about it!  Think about playing halo or othe FPS in the comfort of your recliner.  With 9ft cables on the controller.  Not having to be secluded when using the PC.  Its much more social.  well anyway I really like my new system.  Wether you do or not is your decision.  Who ends up missin out on a good time in the end?||||reg||1
Z||000031||p4n1c||11-19-2001||02:31 PM||||Actually I can recline just fine on my couch in front of the TV with my PC.  It's called TV out.  I've had it in all my video cards.  Also it's not just some of the games that are going to be buggy it's the OS that is the main concern.  Microsoft's track records with OS is bad, and it's going to be just the same.<P>I agree their joysticks and mice have gradually gotten better through the years, after updates and everything else.  The X-box is going to be the same, but gamers aren't as forgiving as the average home PC user.<P>The graphics are not better!  I have played the damn system, since people seem to think I haven't.  They look like anything else released on the PC.  I just have to slap a GeForce3 in my PC or a Radeon 8500.  From what I saw they look no more better then what I can get out of my GeForce2 with everything cranked, except the hardware vertex shading and the higher resolutions.<P>I'm not missing out on any good times.  I have ten times more games on the PC, I've been to LAN parties with it, where we had a lot more then 4 people playing.  And most patches are not for hardware issues for Microsoft, they are OS issues.<P>There is a certain program you can compile in VC++ that crashes XP and 2000, blue screen and shuts down the harddrives.  It's a simple printf doing a couple of tabs and a backspace.  If this kernel is based on 2000, I bet the same exploit works.<P>The hardware is probably rock solid, I know Intel and nVidia make good hardware, it's the OS that is going to irritate most hardcore gamers.  Hell I'd buy one if they can get Linux on it.  Cheap linux workstation.||||reg||1
Z||000032||falconhulk||11-19-2001||02:45 PM||||The OS is not a real windows OS.  It handles limited low level HW calls.  It cant casue the kind of problems you are afraid of.  Did the DC??  You know the DC ran Wince right?  The current crop of games were developed and coded on PC.  They did not have the Debug stations in time.  What you see are direct PC ports pretty much.  Now that the developers have the HW to use the games will show you what the system are capable of.  I have TV out also on my videocard.  Thing is I used it like that for abou 1 week.  PC text looks like crap on TV.  Its a hassle to boot up.  You need to install games.  You need to do the evil patches you refer to.  1 year later you HW is outdated. A new video card costs as much as the xbox.  ||||reg||1
Z||000033||p4n1c||11-19-2001||02:48 PM||||There's another good point.  The X-Box is actually already obsolete.  How are you going to upgrade it?  When the games get so highend, they won't work on the system and you'll have to buy another one, instead of just swapping a processor or video card.<P>[Edit:]<P>Also how did the X-Box crash at the kiosks?  Would it be OS problems?  It's not just low level HW calls it makes, how does it play audio CDs or DVDs?  It has applications running on top of the operating system.  And the Dreamcast ran a WinCE <B>compatible</B> OS, not WinCE itself, read the front of the machine.  It also has to send error codes and debugging information.  I've already seen the "green" screen of death on Slashdot.<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000034||falconhulk||11-19-2001||03:54 PM||||The xbox crashed becasue the game demos were using old versions of the video and audio drivers.  xbox will not be outdated until its outdated.  Console life is usually 5 years.  Xbox power has not even been tapped yet.  We will see its true power in a few months.  Like I said, programers can do a whole lot when the platform is stable and never changing.  Why do you think that consoles are so popular?  Its more profitable to develop for and the development cycles are much shorter.  To me the xbox represents all the benifits of a PC and a console.  Its been said its the easiest console to develop for.  Developers with PC experiance already have the knowledge to make xbox games.  They just need to learn the tweaks that truly make the xbox version stand out.  ||||reg||1
Z||000035||falconhulk||11-19-2001||04:00 PM||||BTW, Dc ran WINCE.  Some games were programed completely in Wince.  It had Wince and a completely low level HW OS proprietary to sega.  I had the system.  I can safely say I am an expert on it.  I have torn it apart.  I have coded simple games like pong for it.  Hmmmm you did know it was possible to make your own games for DC? You are correct as far as cd's and dvd's but hey how much work do you think its doing?  Since i just got the system and there is not a whole lot of info I cant say how complicated the apps are.  It may not be anymore so then your standard DVD or cd player!  ||||reg||1
Z||000036||p4n1c||11-19-2001||04:16 PM||||The OSs in X-Box and DC are not low level at all, they have a low level APIs to interface with hardware(X-Box I believe uses a certain version of DirectX(which is why the games are going to be no more feature rich then PC)).  They have GUI calls to make, debugging info if turned on, system setup, TCP/IP stack setup(for the NIC), etc.<P>Also the X-Box has changed, according to 84fierotrevor, the demo unit was not the same as the real unit shipped and I saw a unit at a MechWarrior 4 tourney that I was in, in the summer.  Some kid won it(they just showed the system and it looks like it does now, he didn't receive it until probably when it was released).  And I thought nothing would have to be patched, but you just said there was buggy video and audio drivers. hmmm.||||reg||1
Z||000037||falconhulk||11-19-2001||04:30 PM||||They were old non shipping drivers.  I dont understand you.  You are trying as hard as possible to discredit this system.  If the system is like the DC then there are no GUI call in game.  They are programed by the developer.  There are GUI calls when booted without game but so what????  Whats your definition of low level?  Low level is hardware level.  IP stack is low level.  Sure there are some minor apps that run.  But these apps are WELL documented for all developers!  There ill not be 100 open apps running all the time in the background as with PC windows.  The Os has deliberately been dumbed down to eliminate problems.  The xbox went through many diffrent versions.  Most of which were mocked up Pc's.  They were demo units.  Yes the Xbox uses direct x.  So do all your PC games.  The version of directx had conflicts with the older HW in the demo units.  I have Munch, DOA3, and halo.  Trust me when I say there is NO slowdown or long loadtimes.  I have played it for hours with no problem.  You have your mind made up. Fine dont buy it.  But like I said I like it.  I would recommend it.  Its a great system.  I dont say this out of being a MS fanboy.  I am 26 years old.  Been playing games since Colecovision.  I am a Network Eng., went to school for Electronic Eng.  I know HW and SW.  The system may not succed but I will have fun while it lasts.  The same as with the DC.<p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000038||p4n1c||11-19-2001||05:55 PM||||I'm 21 and a Computer Network Engineering Technician and work for AT&T.  I've been playing games since my TRS-80 when I was 3 and programming off and on since I was 12. That has nothing do with anything.  <P>That fact of the matter is, is that Microsoft and software don't mix, they'll find someway to screw it up.  It's taken how long for DirectX to actually start to become a somewhat good API?||||reg||1
