o are you talking to?  Me or FirstFiero?  And second, I said they MADE memory cards for it THAT IS WHY THE HARDDRIVE IS USED FOR PATCHES.  Learn to read.  And while you're learning to read, learn to spell.  Also do not call me stupid, I'm quite intelligent and like to join an argument every now and then, because it's fun for a boring day at work.  I don't feel the need to use profanity with every sentence.  And for upgrades I'm not talking 32x or other lame devices like that, I'm talking processors, video cards.  If you're going to build a system with off the shelf parts, might as well make it upgradable.<P>And I don't own a GameCube, nor do I own an X-Box.  I won't buy either, because I will grow bored with them.  As I did with the N64, Dreamcast, Genesis, the PS I never touched because I got bored just renting it.<P>I never said anything about GameSpot either, again learn to read.  It's that thing you learn to do in elementary school, you know?  Books?  Stuff like that?<P>[EDIT:]<BR>And people just don't listen.  The GeForce3 has faster clock/core speeds, which allows it to push more triangles per second down the rendering pipeline, so of course it can render Pixar quality graphics at somewhat decent framerates.<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
