Z||000063||falconhulk||11-21-2001||01:05 PM||||Wrong Lou.  The xbox is absolutely the most powerful console ever made.  Check this site out.  Its an independent educational site that explains everything from autos to crayons.  They break the systems down by specs and xbos is definitely on top.  No bias here.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.howstuffworks.com/xbox.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.howstuffworks.com/xbox.htm</A><P>Also about the emulator....wrong again.  Everytime a new console launches there are rumors of emulation software being built in.  Sega was supposedly going  to include PS1 emulation but did not due to Sonys threats .  They are rumors and nothing else.  There is a diffrence between fact an fiction.  I wish a lot of the people who posted to this topic actually tried to find evidence of what they are saying on the net.  Not rumor but proof.  <p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000064||lou_dias||11-23-2001||09:46 AM||||Quote from how stuff works:<BR>"It should be pointed out that the PlayStation 2 and Xbox figures are theoretical top speeds -- it's unlikely that your system will reach that limit. Nintendo's figure is considered a more realistic number for its console. "<P>Look, I am not trying to start a flame but a P3 is an 8 bit processor hack and slashed to look 32bit with 32 bit inputs where a PPC chip is a true 32bit processor.  Also, a PPC can process more instuctions per clock cyle than ANY x86 based CPU.  Also, the graphics chip in the GameCube is based on the ATI Radeon which as we know is better than NVidia.  About 2 years ago, the goal for a top of the line Graphics processor was 1 million polygons per second.  Do you think in 2 years they've gone from 1 million to 125 million?  With that logic, why don't we have 125 Ghz Pentiums right now?<P>Anyway, the heart of any system (computer or game machine) is it's CPU and the Cube's is stronger.  There are plenty of websites that compare Pentiums to PPC chips and it basically a PPC is 2.5 times faster than a pentium at the same clockspeed.  If the cube only had a 350mhz CPU then things would be tougher, but is has a 475Mhz cpu and that makes it equal to a 1187 Mhz P3.  If you still think that the chip compensates for that gap, my AMD 800 Slot A with a ATI Radeon 64MB DDR is slower than my AMD 900 Slot A Thuderbird w/Voodoo 3500.  Now Voodoo is what 3-4 years old?  Yet my 900 system plays games in 32bit 1280x1024 screen modes plenty fast.  And yes, my 800 system is faster than the Xbox.||||reg||1
Z||000065||GTFiero1||11-23-2001||11:00 AM||||so your saying a web site that has nothing to gain by lieing lied? it says that ps2 has 70million polygons per second and the Game cube has 12million polygons per second. so your putting down all the systems....It should be pointed out that the PlayStation 2 and Xbox figures are theoretical top speeds -- it's unlikely that your system will reach that limit.... yes but that means that its in the general area or 125mil and 70mil<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<P>you gotta keep on keepin on...||||reg||1
Z||000066||lou_dias||11-23-2001||12:25 PM||||Sony lost the lawsuit against BLEEM! but then bought the company.  During that time, Sony changed it's CDs so that BLEEM! or any other emulator couldn't play the NEWEST games.  Again Sega would have made money selling an emulation CD but it was useless for new hot games so who would buy it?  and again it would be giving money to Sony buy increasing their game sales.  By the way, there was a BLEEM for the Dreamcast that let it play games.  So it wasn't a Sega-made product but someone else's.  They could have easily made an XBOX Bleem to play PS1 games but guess what BLEEM is not dead.  <A HREF="http://www.bleem.com" TARGET=_blank>www.bleem.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000067||loafer87gt||11-23-2001||01:20 PM||||Hey Lou, check out your link man. Bleem went tits up last week. As far as the consoles go, I don't care what system has the better hardware, I'll be getting whatever system has the best games. I'm going to wait a couple of months and see how much support the GC gets, I was already bitten by teh n64, and don't really want to waste my money on another sytem with little or no games. I think the X-Box will be good for PC gamers however, as games should be easy to port over and will finally have support for us GF3 owners.||||reg||1
